Box 7-2: Well’s Scoring for DVT probability
The Well’s scoring system for DVT probability objectifies clinical suspicion of 
DVT risk and provides criteria for initiating treatment.  
The presence or absence of the clinical features below are computed to give a 
pre-testing probability score for that particular patient which is used to priori­
tise investigation and treatment. 
yy
Paralysis, paresis or recent orthopedic casting of lower extremity (1 point)
yy
Recently bedridden (more than 3 days) or major surgery within past 4 
weeks (1 point)
yy
Localized tenderness in deep vein system (1 point)
yy
Swelling of entire leg (1 point)
yy
Calf swelling 3 cm greater than other leg (measured 10 cm below the tibial 
tuberosity) (1 point)
yy
Pitting oedema greater in the symptomatic leg (1 point)
yy
Collateral non varicose superficial veins (1 point)
yy
Active cancer or cancer treated within 6 months (1 point)
yy
Alternative diagnosis more likely than DVT (Baker’s cyst, cellulitis, muscle 
damage, superficial venous thrombosis, post phlebitic syndrome, inguinal 
lymphadenopathy, external venous compression) (-2 points)
