68.	 The Unconscious Patient
Unconsciousness is a common clinical problem and may be associated 
with diseases of several organs in the body. The cause of unconsciousness 
is often not immediately evident, and a systematic approach to its 
diagnosis and management is therefore important. Obtaining a thorough 
history from accompanying relatives, friends and the police is essential.
