70.	 The Acutely Disturbed Patient
The acutely disturbed patient presents in an excited, agitated or 
aggressive state. There may be delusions and perceptual changes like 
hallucinations that overwhelm the patient. Disorientation and alteration 
in consciousness are often prominent when the cause is organic.  The 
patients are usually brought in restrained by more than one person or by 
the police. The condition must be regarded as an emergency since a few 
cases are potentially fatal.
Causes 
Acute (Functional) Psychiatric Disorders
